WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.160
As Boba Fett, Temuera Morrison is one&nbsp;
of the most feared men in the galaxy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:07.040
But back home in New Zealand,&nbsp;
why is he still overshadowed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.720
even more famous members of his own&nbsp;
family? Keep watching to find out!

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.280
Temuera Morrison's artistic lineage can&nbsp;
be traced to his uncle Howard Morrison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.200
a legendary musician in New Zealand whose&nbsp;
success and voice was so wide-reaching that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.360
he was knighted. Beyond his music, which was&nbsp;
popular across the South Pacific and Asia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:27.200
Sir Howard dedicated his time and effort to&nbsp;
fighting for civil rights. In particular,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.040
he rallied for equal education and access&nbsp;
for New Zealand's native Māori people.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.520
Per NZ on Screen, Morrison recalled of his uncle,

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.520
"I remember as a young boy, growing up — we&nbsp;
were always told to stand up and make a speech,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.800
stand up and sing a song, do this&nbsp;
and do that, and when I look back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.120
he was grooming us, training us for our journey."

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.960
However, according to a biography of&nbsp;
Sir Howard written by his son Howie Jr.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.360
the relationship between uncle and nephew might&nbsp;
not have always been smooth. According to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.280
Rotorua Daily Post, the book revealed that&nbsp;
Sir Howard didn't want to share the limelight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:59.440
and criticized Temuera for his breakout role&nbsp;
in the acclaimed film "Once Were Warriors."

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.000
During an interview with Stuff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.520
Temuera Morrison recounted that after&nbsp;
being tapped to play famed Australian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:10.560
rugby coach Eddie Jones in the 2019 film "The&nbsp;
Brighton Miracle," he told director Max Mannix,

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.120
"Are you sure? I am a Māori&nbsp;
from Rotorua, New Zealand."

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:16.080
The Māori are thought to have arrived&nbsp;
in New Zealand about a thousand years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.880
ago as members of the Polynesian peoples whose&nbsp;
ocean-going exploits are epic. And as a Māori,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:25.600
Morrison is part of a collection of successful&nbsp;
Polynesian actors blowing open doors in Hollywood.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:29.360
This list includes several A-listers&nbsp;
working today. From action stars like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:32.320
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson to "Masked&nbsp;
Singer" judge Nicole Scherzinger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.400
the rise of entertainers of Polynesian descent&nbsp;
has been a great stride for inclusiveness.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.520
Temuera Morrison is named after his grandfather,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:43.520
who was a professional rugby player.&nbsp;
Morrison told Rotorua Daily Post,

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.920
"My cousin Terry Tapsell was born a week after me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.920
whichever one was born first was going to be&nbsp;
called Temuera after our Morrison grandfather."

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.280
Grandpa Morrison was a member of the&nbsp;
New Zealand rugby squad All Blacks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:58.240
the perennial kings of the rugby pitch. But the&nbsp;
team isn't without its controversies. Sir Howard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.880
with his group the Howard Morrison Quartet,&nbsp;
memorialized one such incident involving his dad.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.040
Their hit 1960 protest song, "My Old Man's&nbsp;
an All Black" is about how the team wasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:11.200
allowed to play its Māori members for a&nbsp;
tournament in apartheid-era South Africa.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.560
Plenty has changed since then, and the&nbsp;
All Blacks have gained global fame for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:19.280
performing a pregame haka, a traditional Māori&nbsp;
dance focused on intimidating the opponent.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.000
The average American filmgoer likely didn't&nbsp;
have any idea who Temuera Morrison was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.840
before he appeared as Jango Fett and&nbsp;
then all of Jango's clones. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.280
by the time he joined the Star Wars universe,&nbsp;
he had already been nominated for several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:34.960
awards and even won a few trophies for&nbsp;
acting work in his native New Zealand.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:40.080
His portrayal of Jake "The Muss" Heke in the 1994&nbsp;
Kiwi hit "Once Were Warriors" made him a household&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.760
name back home. But during an interview with&nbsp;
Stuff, Morrison revealed that the fame he earned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:47.600
through that project wasn't everything it was&nbsp;
cracked up to be, describing the role as a, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.120
"millstone" around his neck, and expressing&nbsp;
displeasure with the making of the film.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:55.280
"It was a lot of hard work and emotional mayhem.&nbsp;
[...] People go nutty doing movies like that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:58.160
It was full-on and [we] never knew&nbsp;
how it was going to turn out."

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:02.320
The hard work paid off, however, as Morrison&nbsp;
won a New Zealand Film and TV Award for "Best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:06.640
Performance in a Dramatic Role" for "Once Were&nbsp;
Warriors" and would later earn a "Best Actor" win&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:11.200
for his reprisal of Jake in the film's sequel,&nbsp;
1999's "What Becomes of the Broken Hearted?"

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:15.120
The original "Star Wars" movies had a&nbsp;
few instances where one actor filled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.760
the suit while another voiced&nbsp;
it. One of these was, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:21.440
Boba Fett, with Jeremy Bulloch wearing&nbsp;
the suit and Jason Wingreen delivering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:24.640
the voicework for Boba Fett's four&nbsp;
lines in "The Empire Strikes Back."

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:29.120
After Temuera Morrison played Jango Fett&nbsp;
in body and voice in 2002's "Attack of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.920
the Clones," it made sense that&nbsp;
he was tapped to play Boba Fett&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.160
in "The Mandalorian" and "The Book of Boba&nbsp;
Fett," since Boba Fett is a clone of Jango.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:41.520
That raised an issue though: Morrions's voice is&nbsp;
obviously different from Wingreen's. So in 2004,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.800
LucasFilm brought Morrison back&nbsp;
to re-record all of Boba's lines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:47.360
in "The Empire Strikes Back" for future releases.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.120
At least there's only one Jango!

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:50.640
"There's only one Jango, and that's me!"

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:55.120
Temuera Morrison had long wanted to&nbsp;
return to the Star Wars universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:59.040
even saying in 2017 that he'd&nbsp;
want to play an older Captain Rex,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:03.920
another clone of Jango Fett who was introduced&nbsp;
in the 2008 animated film "Clone Wars."

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.600
Of course, that led to wild speculation that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:09.040
Morrison might actually be able to&nbsp;
some day portray Boba Fett himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:13.040
even though Fett seemingly died in "The&nbsp;
Return of the Jedi." A pipe dream, right?

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:16.240
Well, that dream came true and Morrison&nbsp;
brought the bounty hunter back to life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:20.560
in "The Mandalorian," albeit as an older&nbsp;
Boba Fett, one who survived escaping from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:24.560
the giant stomach of the Sarlacc. After&nbsp;
that ordeal and the ravages of time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:27.600
it was inevitable that the actor would&nbsp;
have to shed his rugged good looks and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.280
smooth voice in order to portray a&nbsp;
scarred, battle-worn, older Boba.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:35.040
Discussing his role in "The&nbsp;
Mandalorian," Morrison told StarWars.com,

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.800
"I did rely a lot on the makeup. [...] I spent&nbsp;
a lot of the time sitting in the makeup chair,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:42.240
watching what was being applied, and then&nbsp;
things just started to happen organically."

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.400
Regarding his vocal changes, Morrison said,

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.120
"I thought, every now and then he&nbsp;
hit some tonal qualities where,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:50.880
hey, he has been scarred. He has been&nbsp;
affected internally, as well. So without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:54.480
sounding too false I wanted to bring a little&nbsp;
gravel in there to give it a bit of timbre."

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:59.280
The United Kingdom and its commonwealth&nbsp;
nations, including New Zealand, still view&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:04.000
Queen Elizabeth II as their queen despite&nbsp;
political independence. Along those lines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:08.320
titles and nobility are bestowed on New Zealand&nbsp;
citizens just like in England. In New Zealand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:12.640
the nation's Royal Honours system gives titles&nbsp;
and names people to various orders and honours.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:16.880
As his bio explains, Temuera Morrison was&nbsp;
named to the New Zealand Order of Merit for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:21.440
services to drama in a 1996 Queen's Birthday&nbsp;
Honours. While he was named as a Member,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:26.080
there are further levels to achieve. At the top&nbsp;
are the titles of Dame and Knight, the level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:30.960
attained by his uncle Howard Morrison, therefore&nbsp;
also known as Sir Howard. Perhaps Knighthood is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:34.880
destined for Morrison if he continues to&nbsp;
captivate audiences with his acting chops.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:37.040
Plus, considering Boba Fett's signature helmet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:40.480
looks like something worn by a medieval&nbsp;
knight, it appears to be his destiny!

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:45.840
Temuera Morrison is an imposing guy. He earned&nbsp;
accolades for playing the violent Jake "The Muss"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:49.840
Heke and went on to play two of the most savage&nbsp;
bounty hunters in the history of the galaxy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:53.680
But Morrison likes to also mix things up&nbsp;
and show his softer side once in a while.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:58.240
"It'll be nice to play just a nice man for a&nbsp;
change without all the hullabalooey stuff."

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:02.560
Luckily, voice acting helps with that. Of&nbsp;
course, he did voice Jango and Boba Fett,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:05.520
both in the films and also in&nbsp;
video games like the "Star Wars:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:09.280
Battlefront" series. But he also voiced&nbsp;
the more nurturing Chief Tui in "Moana,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:13.120
the Disney sensation with a cast list that&nbsp;
features an all-star ensemble of the world's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:16.880
biggest Polynesian actors and actresses.&nbsp;
Morrison is joined by Dwayne Johnson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:21.280
Jemaine Clement, Auli'i Cravalho, and Nicole&nbsp;
Scherzinger among others in the hit movie.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.040
Given his distinctively tough voice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:26.640
we can only hope he continues to talk&nbsp;
behind the camera as well as in front of it.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:30.480
In 2009, Temuera Morrison&nbsp;
penned his autobiography,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:33.920
"From Haka to Hollywood." Morrison told&nbsp;
the New Zealand Sunday News that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:36.720
hoped that his book "will inspire&nbsp;
others to reach for the stars."

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:40.880
Like many celebrity autobiographies, it was&nbsp;
ghost-written, in this case by Paul Little.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:42.960
Morrison told the New Zealand Sunday News,

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:45.920
"I'm just going to talk a lot and Paul&nbsp;
is going to try and make something out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.800
of it. [...] Before moving to Auckland&nbsp;
I used to perform professionally in my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:51.920
Māori culture groups [...] I believe&nbsp;
there's a formula to getting to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:55.680
top and by talking in this book I might&nbsp;
reveal how the haka I got to Hollywood."

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:01.520
Temuera Morrison is a man of many talents. Acting&nbsp;
and voice acting are just the tip of the iceberg.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:06.000
While his uncle Sir Howard is one of New Zealand's&nbsp;
most popular musicians of all time, Morrison's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:11.040
father, Laurie, was a musician as well. So it's&nbsp;
no surprise that in 2014 Morrison released his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:16.080
own album, "Tem," which features covers of classic&nbsp;
songs his dad and uncle liked and used to perform.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:19.600
In an interview with Radio New Zealand,&nbsp;
Morrison explained how he used to listen to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:22.880
his father's records. He also mentioned&nbsp;
that when his dad came home from work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.720
he'd shine the old man's shoes before his&nbsp;
father went to perform at a venue in Auckland.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:31.200
It's fun to imagine the elder Morrisons jamming&nbsp;
out to American classics, and it's impressive how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:35.680
good Temuera covers songs ranging from "Midnight&nbsp;
Special" to "It's Not Unusual" on the album.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:39.520
Morrison also had another entertainment&nbsp;
gig, hosting his own TV shows, one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:42.960
which he believes might have inspired&nbsp;
his record deal. Morrison told Stuff,

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:46.320
"I think Sony must have seen my [TV&nbsp;
variety show] 'Happy Hour' at 9:30&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.200
p.m. on TV One. They said: 'Why not do an album?'"

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:53.520
His hosting career may not have lasted long but he&nbsp;
did get George Lucas to appear on his talk show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:57.600
"The Tem Show." Not bad for a simple man&nbsp;
trying to make his way in the galaxy.

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:00.880
"Thank you also for cloning me! There's&nbsp;
only me and a sheep called Dolly, I think!"

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:07.040
It's a common adage that being a child actor&nbsp;
does not necessarily lead to a successful adult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:11.840
career. Luckily Temuera Morrison, whose first&nbsp;
onscreen appearance was at the tender age of 11,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:17.440
bucked the trend. According to NZ On Screen,&nbsp;
he was cast as a main character Rangi in 1973's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:22.560
"Rangi's Catch" after director Michael Forlong&nbsp;
spotted him performing for tourists in Rotorua.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:27.040
In the movie, he plays a kid who, along with&nbsp;
three others, pursues two escaped convicts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:30.400
Catherine de la Roche, who reviewed the&nbsp;
film for "Dominion" said it was, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.480
"one of the best children's films ever made."

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:37.520
His next credit wasn't until 11 years later,&nbsp;
at the age of 22, playing a Rasta street kid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:42.000
on the New Zealand TV series "Mortimer's Patch."&nbsp;
Two years later he would get recurring roles on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:46.400
two other New Zealand TV series, "Seekers"&nbsp;
and "Adventurer." From there, Morrison began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:50.960
that long journey to playing Jango Fett and&nbsp;
blasting onto movie screens all over the world.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:56.400
Temuera Morrison's first character to reach a&nbsp;
global audience was Jake in "Once Were Warriors."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:00.560
And his performance impressed no less than&nbsp;
legendary American film critic Roger Ebert.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.240
In his review of the film, Ebert wrote,

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:05.920
"In Temuera Morrison, as Jake, the movie&nbsp;
finds a leading actor as elemental,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:10.080
charismatic and brutal as the young Marlon&nbsp;
Brando; he has instinctive star power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:13.680
and it's his likability that makes the&nbsp;
violence of his character so shocking."

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:17.840
Morrison mentioned in a 2014 interview with&nbsp;
Screen-Space that to prepare for the film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:21.040
he was instructed to watch Brando's&nbsp;
performance as Stanley Kowalski in "A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:25.760
Streetcar Named Desire," so Ebert's comparison&nbsp;
certainly makes sense. What was unexpected,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:29.280
though, is that Morrison would end up&nbsp;
co-starring with the legendary Brando.

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:33.200
"The Island of Dr. Moreau" starred Brando&nbsp;
as the title mad scientist in a film that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:37.840
got quite a few negative reviews. Morrison,&nbsp;
who played man-dog hybrid Azazello, told&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:42.400
Screen-Space that he left the shoot because it&nbsp;
was dragging on, before a lawyer forced him back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:46.800
Still, Morrison fondly recalls sharing the screen&nbsp;
with one of his idols, telling Rotten Tomatoes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:49.520
"it was great to see him work, see a master work."

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.240
No doubt, some day an up-and-comer&nbsp;
will say that same thing in an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:55.280
interview about the time they got&nbsp;
to work alongside Morrison himself.

